! Step 7 — grant authority boundary prepared; controller test wall

`res-005` succeeded: the lane head now reads `cd299ae214d92f118a12a77676eb1048acf23d0b`. `relay/req-006.json` requests a lane commit of the mesh cure and its retirement test at that head. Read its receipt next step; do not advance the recorded head ahead of that receipt. The supplied controller report says the two mesh files passed 17/17; no raw run log or blind custody review was available in this lane. A lane commit does not land a slice on the span. Blind Opus custody review and the authority-caller blockers remain before land.

The uncommitted grant work requires a pinned-root-incepted persona KEL and a founder-specific remove-wins dyad result before `verifyFaceGrantRecord` accepts. It refuses absent proof by name, aside and unknown/owing; clear and returned may proceed. The join writer takes a separate founder proof, checks its lineage and standing before provider mutation, and passes it into the standing grant reader. The daemon obtains the founder's dyad separately from the joinee's; the ring supplies its fail-closed device shadow. The seat obtains the founder reading and does not permanently memoize a missing-proof refusal. These changes have not run or received custody review. The KEL inception pin alone does ''not'' prove a non-rolled-back frontier or a complete fleet view.

