Fork: 🜁 philosopher separates a founder's authority from the joinee's; 🜄 weighs a temporarily unavailable join against seating under another device's standing. The latter can transfer authority after removal, so the former refuses without the founder's own reading. The local frontier cannot reveal an unseen removal: applying remove-wins on receipt, complete-view census, sealed anti-rollback, and restart safety remain owed. Early-alpha re-genesis permits burning legacy fields only in the coordinated final cut, while the current lease guard stays until the reader census proves coverage.

